# Scratch-file patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern with no
# slash matches at ANY depth: a bare junit.xml in a product .gitignore silently
# excluded a required committed fixture in P060 of this mission, and a cold
# clone then failed with 17 failures and 9 errors while every local check
# passed. validation/validate_tree_hygiene.py checks both directions with
# `git check-ignore`: that nothing this product must ship is excluded, and that
# every cache and build path is.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.pytest_cache/
/.hypothesis/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
/.config/
# Model checkpoints. This product ships no serialised model: the learned
# predictor is a random forest refitted from the committed traces in under a
# second, and a pickled estimator would bind the repository to one
# scikit-learn build whose unpickling is not part of that library's public API.
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.joblib
# The MEASURED traces are NOT ignored. data/traces/*.csv, manifest.json and the
# campaign's own markers are the product's evidence and must reach a cold clone.
# They are listed as negations so that a future broad pattern cannot swallow
# them silently.
!/data/traces/
!/data/traces/*.csv
!/data/traces/manifest.json
!/data/traces/CAMPAIGN_COMPLETE
